&lt;td style=&quot;border: 1px solid black; padding: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;05/08/2009:&lt;/strong&gt; During a routine credentials renewal, Dr. K. Elstrom speaks her 43NET password aloud via telephone to Identification and Technocryptography (I&amp;amp;T) technician W. Barkley. Barkley asks Dr. Elstrom to confirm the password by repeating it; she finds herself unable to do so. Dr. Elstrom asks that Barkley instead repeat the password back to her; when he refuses, citing protocol, she becomes extremely agitated and demands to speak to his supervisor.&lt;/td&gt;
